  "notes": "Fitaihi Holding Group Company (ticker 4180, a Saudi Joint Stock Company, Jeddah) audited consolidated financial statements for the year ended 31 December 2025 with FY2024 comparatives, from the full audited PDF in the 'Annual / 2025' cell of the Saudi Exchange company-profile 'Financial Statements' tab (Resources/fsPdf/453_0_2026-03-19...). Auditor: El Sayed El Ayouty & Co. (Moore network; Abdullah A. Balamesh, licence 345); unqualified opinion, dated Jeddah 10 March 2026. The consolidated financial statements were approved by the Board of Directors on 10 March 2026 (corresponding to 21 Ramadan 1447H) - Note 28. Amounts are presented in full Saudi Riyals (scale 1). The auditor's report and the primary statements (printed FS pages 1-5) are scanned images in the filed PDF (transcribed from page renders at 2.7x); the notes are digital text. Fitaihi is a holding group - its jewellery / luxury-retail operations run an operating LOSS (SAR -8.4m FY2025 / -7.9m FY2024) and the Group's earnings come from an equity-accounted associate (investments_associates SAR 194.1m; its main investment) and from FVOCI-equity dividends. Consolidated with a subsidiary but there is **NO non-controlling interest** (net profit and equity are not split), so only total_equity is carried. There are no discontinued operations - the standard pre-tax - zakat bridge applies. investments_associates is 'Investment in an associate company'; long_term_investments is 'Investments in equity instruments at fair value through other comprehensive income'; other_reserves combines the 'Statutory reserve', the 'Reserve in equity instruments at fair value through OCI' and the 'Reserve of cashflows hedge of the associate company'. **The Group has no bank debt** - the only liabilities are lease liabilities ('Liabilities for right-of-use assets', carried as lease_liabilities_noncurrent / lease_liabilities_current), trade payables, EOSB and zakat. accounts_receivable is 'Trade and other receivables'; accounts_payable is 'Trade and other payables'; defined_benefit_obligation is 'Employees defined benefit obligations'; zakat_payable is 'Provision for zakat'. On the P&L: operating_income is 'Loss from operation'; share_of_profit_associates is 'Company's share of the business result of the associate company'; dividend_income is 'Dividend from equity instrument at fair value through other comprehensive income'; finance_costs is 'Finance costs - lease liabilities'; other_income is 'Other income / (expenses) - Net'; income_taxes_and_zakat is the 'Zakat' charge. On the cash-flow statement: depreciation_amortization combines PP&E and right-of-use-asset depreciation; zakat_paid is 'Zakat paid'; capex is 'Payments for additions to property and equipment'; dividends_paid is 'Dividends paid' (FY2025 only); lease_payments is 'Liabilities and debit interest paid for lease contracts' (lease principal plus lease interest); the cash-flow statement has no separate finance-cost-paid line so interest_paid is not carried, and it has no FX-on-cash line; its closing balance equals the balance-sheet 'Cash and cash equivalents' line exactly. FY2025: net profit SAR 4.0m (FY2024 SAR 14.5m - which included a much larger associate contribution), EPS 0.015. Statement page references are the printed FS page numbers: financial position 1, profit or loss 2, comprehensive income 3, changes in equity 4, cash flows 5.",
